Sadly this game is not recomended after you play great quality ARPG.
In short: only buy if you don`t mind to play a generic MMO style punched into a single player game.
Positives:
+ Interesting visual alert when your heath is low;
+ Music and Blind Guardian (their music blends with the "animus" of ARPG);
+ Unique characters to play, including good and evil oriented;
+ Nice graphics and runs in 2560 x 1080 (to people with ultra-wide);
+ They tried to make a funny game.
Negatives:
- Huge map plagued with non stop monsters spawn (rats...kobolts);
- Repetitive quests: it`s 500 of boredom;
- No sense of real progression;
- Weak story;
- At glance, the open world is a twist but with time, the game can`t uphold the player interested.

H1Z1;
H1Z1 is a overall ok game with some flaws but them flaws are bearable. The patches that are coming out are ok. the one that i realy liked was the gun remodeling one. now the guns feel and look better than before, the ADS looks cleaner and now the shotgun isnt as OP as before. still it is slightly broken but it is good overall. The game itself feels a little wonkey in some areas. I couldnt compare this game to PUBG because PUBG is very different to H1Z1. PUBG feels more realistic and handles different. However H1Z1 has a more of a rushed pace to the game. Basicaly if you want a slower paced but more realistic survival game then go for PUBG, but pick it up in the sale because £27 is to much for the game. However H1Z1 (as of writing this review) is now £3.74. I would recommend picking this game up and trying it but its your decision realy.
Overall this game is a ok game but needs some tweaks with the preformance and some other issues. Id give this game a 7/10

